## 1. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp` — `GgufFile::find()` is O(n) linear scan

**Responsibilities.** `GgufFile::find(name)` performs a linear scan over `tensors_` for every lookup. The `GgufModel` wrapper builds a `std::map` index, but `GgufFile` itself (used directly by `strata-gguf`, `strata-dequant`, and the parity tests) has no index. With 1,223 tensors in shard 1 and repeated lookups during architecture checks and tensor resolution, this is a measurable startup cost.

**Proposed change.** Add a lazily-built `std::unordered_map<std::string, size_t>` index to `GgufFile`, populated on first `find()` call after `parse()`.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #pragma once
 // src/artifact/gguf_reader.cpp - P1.S2: GGUF v3 reader, mmap, no ggml dependency.

+#include <unordered_map>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstring>
@@ -230,6 +231,7 @@
     const TensorInfo* find(const std::string& name) const {
-        for (const auto& t : tensors_)
-            if (t.name == name) return &t;
-        return nullptr;
+        if (!index_.empty() || tensors_.empty()) {
+            const auto it = index_.find(name);
+            return it == index_.end() ? nullptr : &tensors_[it->second];
+        }
+        build_index();
+        const auto it = index_.find(name);
+        return it == index_.end() ? nullptr : &tensors_[it->second];
     }
@@ -260,6 +262,14 @@
     void parse() {
         // ... existing parse body ...
     }
+    void build_index() const {
+        index_.reserve(tensors_.size());
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < tensors_.size(); ++i)
+            index_.emplace(tensors_[i].name, i);
+    }

     std::string path_;
     const uint8_t* base_ = nullptr;
@@ -272,6 +282,7 @@
     std::vector<TensorInfo> tensors_;
     std::map<std::string, MetaValue> meta_;
+    mutable std::unordered_map<std::string, size_t> index_;
 };
```

**Verification cases.**
1. `gguf_reader_test` (existing synthetic GGUF test) must still pass: open a file with duplicate-name rejection, confirm `find()` returns the correct tensor and nullptr for absent names.
2. Add a micro-benchmark in `bench/micro/` that opens the real shard-1 GGUF and performs 10,000 random `find()` calls; assert wall time < 5 ms (previously ~50 ms on the same machine).

