## 2. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp` — `GgufModel::find()` stores dangling `const TensorInfo*` into `shards_[i]->tensors()`

**Responsibilities.** `GgufModel` builds `index_` mapping name → `(shard_index, const TensorInfo*)`. The pointer points into the `std::vector<TensorInfo>` owned by each `GgufFile`. If a `GgufFile` were ever moved or its vector reallocated, the pointer would dangle. Currently safe because `GgufFile` is non-copyable and `tensors_` is never modified after `parse()`, but the invariant is undocumented and fragile.

**Proposed change.** Store the tensor index within the shard rather than a raw pointer, and resolve through `shards_[i]->tensors()[idx]`.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@
         for (size_t i = 0; i < shards_.size(); ++i)
             for (const auto& t : shards_[i]->tensors()) {
-                const auto ins = index_.emplace(t.name, std::make_pair(i, &t));
+                const auto ins = index_.emplace(t.name, std::make_pair(i, (size_t)(&t - shards_[i]->tensors().data())));
                 if (!ins.second)
                     throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: tensor " + t.name + " is in two shards (" +
                                              shards_[ins.first->second.first]->path() + " and " +
@@ -325,8 +325,8 @@
     const TensorInfo* find(const std::string& name, size_t* shard = nullptr) const {
         const auto it = index_.find(name);
         if (it == index_.end()) return nullptr;
-        if (shard) *shard = it->second.first;
-        return it->second.second;
+        if (shard) *shard = it->second.first;
+        return &shards_[it->second.first]->tensors()[it->second.second];
     }
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@
     std::vector<std::unique_ptr<GgufFile>> shards_;
-    std::map<std::string, std::pair<size_t, const TensorInfo*>> index_;
+    std::map<std::string, std::pair<size_t, size_t>> index_;
 };
```

**Verification cases.**
1. `gguf_split_test` (existing synthetic split-model test) must pass unchanged: open a 2-shard model, look up tensors in both shards, confirm correct shard indices and tensor data.
2. Add a test that constructs a `GgufModel`, copies the returned `TensorInfo*` into a local, then destroys the model — confirm no use-after-free under ASan by verifying the pointer is only used while the model is alive (the new form makes the dependency explicit).

